  "Question": "A team won \\(40\\) of its first \\(50\\) games. How many of the remaining \\(40\\) games must this team win so it will have won exactly \\(70\\%\\) of its games for the season?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(20\\)",
    "B": "\\(23\\)",
    "C": "\\(28\\)",
    "D": "\\(30\\)",
    "E": "\\(35\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "The \\(70\\%\\) applies to the entire season, which has \\(50+40=90\\) games. The required number of wins is therefore\n\\[\n0.70\\times90=63.\n\\]\nThe team already has \\(40\\) wins, so it must win \\(63-40=23\\) of the remaining \\(40\\) games. Thus the answer is \\(23\\), choice B.",
